From 95528f8b1620af16c93745f44eca4b8358a98aa8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "vincent.yen" <vincent.yen@mitaccomputing.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 05:55:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Clean uploaded BIOS activation

The original design may cause the filesystem to become completely full
after multiple BIOS updates because old BIOS image files
in the /tmp/images/ directory are not removed.

Refer to the community implementations in commits
5f1346aff2a3f7bf2cec0cea7e24b9f9acb3a8f2 and 6397c09454cdd43bf901669496763af12c5978b5
to make the following changes.

Clean the uploaded activation after BIOS update completion and after
selected activation failure paths.  For failures, set Activation=Failed
before scheduling cleanup so Redfish task monitoring can observe the
failed state.

Test:
Regardless of whether the BIOS update succeeds or fails,
no stale image should remain in either the D-Bus object path or the /tmp/images directory

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [No upstream maintenance]
